se retain their existing rules.\n\nCurrent review source: `a2483ecc8c43f134f1a1d39661930110eba0033b`, appended normally to the original WI-1089 branch. c960 and every intermediate development commit are preserved. This PR remains **Draft** and the current source is an explicitly intermediate validation state.\n\nActual validation so far:\n\n- The preserved c960 binary reproduces the retained-canonical rejection before the fix. Missing remains a separate baseline.\n- An isolated real-producer fixture keeps the same source snapshot and actual c960 old receipt, then uses the new Linux candidate: exact material record, plan-only with zero processes, four actual passing checks, zero reuse, one worker, fresh green preflight, then actual fixture finish/archive. Original receipt and blocked Outcome bytes remain preserved. This is not the unpublished rc2/macOS Sentinel capsule.\n- Portable changed-source fixtures cover four fresh checks; same-binding tests preserve legitimate four-node reuse and exercise MCP material recording. Twenty-four representative corrupt/foreign/authority mutations plus Unix symlink rejection passed. An actual failed-check cycle and exact native retry also passed.\n- Native six-node attempt1 on `442dd98c` executed every node with zero reuse. Format, all-target clippy, repository status, MCP material and repository material passed. The full CLI suite hit its default 600-second deadline near its last two tests; the suite and overall run are **not passed**. Its structured timeout receipt and logs are retained.\n- The current source hashes the actual immutable candidate identity once per test process, retaining independent per-fixture context clones and actual identity calculation in each spawned CLI. No checks, time limits, product reuse rules or worker limits were relaxed. Native attempt2 is running; format, clippy and repository status have passed, and the full CLI node is in progress. No complete current verification result is claimed yet.\n\nThe native Contract `a5deac9a750543678deff0e444da6e2924976423fb21f419250692c768fc4a69` has an actual recorded `human:Ray confirm_review`. That confirms the amended plan and does not supply the new independent material decision. Current material request `86f59b9be292864b3876adb20306bedd16efc7e6e75a3ab4b7040588704b88d0` contains three new reviewable Rust syntax Unknown blobs, two additional clean Rust implementation files and no Finding. Raydot's exact current material review/authority remains pending; the old finite consent is not reused for changed bytes.\n\nHistorical [c960 CI](https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/actions/runs/39211030001) and [721129 composition CI](https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/actions/runs/39214312107) remain preserved. The latter does not prove composition with this new repair. [Fresh CI39239339866](https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/actions/runs/39239339866) is in progress for the current source. WI1090 and the old combined context remain unchanged. No real Sentinel operation, actual WI finish/archive, merge, Issue closure or cleanup is authorized or claimed. The reported real c960 failure in [#1041](https://github.com/xinglun/ai-cockpit/issues/1041#issuecomment-6263215739) still requires exact local acceptance of the new source.\n\nRefs #1041, #1004.\n","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:57:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T10:43:39Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"31689030aafead65eeaeaec50e617293e50b9484","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/1048/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/1048/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/issues/1048/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xinglun/ai-cockpit/status